# /etc/vpn-failfast.conf
# ======================
# Destinations that are reachable ONLY through the AWS Client VPN tunnel.
#
# While the tunnel is down, scripts/vpn-failfast.sh installs an `unreachable`
# route for each of these, so anything aimed at them fails INSTANTLY instead of
# hanging for the ~127 seconds a TCP SYN takes to give up. When the tunnel
# returns, the routes are withdrawn.
#
# Installed root-owned to /etc/vpn-failfast.conf by `vpn-setup`. Edit the live
# file and then `sudo systemctl restart vpn-failfast` — this repo copy is the
# seed, not the live config, and vpn-doctor will tell you if they have drifted.
#
# ONE DESTINATION PER LINE. IPv4 address or CIDR. `#` starts a comment.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE
# -----------------------------
# The internet, and anything a video call needs. Those keep working over the LAN
# while the tunnel is down — that decision is the whole reason this is a list of
# destinations rather than a default route. Adding a broad prefix here does not
# make the VPN work sooner; it makes everything inside that prefix fail.
#
# THE VALIDATOR WILL REFUSE, and each of these was measured against the real `ip`
# rather than assumed:
#
#   0.0.0.0/0        `ip` ACCEPTS this. It would blackhole the entire internet.
#                    Anything broader than /8 is refused here.
#   10.9.8.1/24      `ip` ACCEPTS this too, and installs the whole /24 — a typo
#                    meant as a host route silently takes 256 addresses with it.
#                    Host bits below the prefix are refused.
#   ::1/128          `ip` ACCEPTS this and installs it into the v6 table. Only
#                    IPv4 is supported here; v6 is refused rather than ignored.
#   127.0.0.1        Loopback. Refused.
#
# A malformed entry makes the unit exit 2 and install NOTHING — never a partial
# set, and never a silent "no destinations", which would be indistinguishable
# from a healthy tunnel.

# The four Quantivly servers, from ~/.ssh/config (the qmux hosts).
54.166.22.221      # dev
44.221.89.155      # staging
23.21.26.91        # demo
3.216.24.205       # qspace

# Add internal CIDRs here as they are discovered. An incomplete list degrades to
# today's behaviour for the missing host — a hang — it never breaks one. Growing
# it is expected: `vpn-sweeps` and ordinary use are what find the gaps.
